    "proseDraft": "The record confirms that all three new templates are live for every customer by Friday 2026-10-30 at 17:00 UK time and that the 2 November campaign links to them. No unresolved items are listed, and the other remarks and requests remain only as stated.\n\nConfirmed by participants\n- Item dev-deadline-end-of-month:item:11 was confirmed by Hannah, Tomasz and Aiko with recheck passed that all three new templates are live for every customer by Friday 2026-10-30 at 17:00 UK time and that the 2 November campaign links to them.\n\nStated in the meeting\n- Item dev-deadline-end-of-month:item:0 was a stated suggestion to aim for end of month for the full switch-over.\n- Item dev-deadline-end-of-month:item:1 was a stated remark about planning around end of month.\n- Item dev-deadline-end-of-month:item:2 was a stated view that end of month should be doable if finance gets back this week.\n- Item dev-deadline-end-of-month:item:3 was a stated remark that finance still owes the wording for reverse charge invoices.\n- Item dev-deadline-end-of-month:item:4 was a stated remark about chasing finance today.\n- Item dev-deadline-end-of-month:item:5 was a stated request to turn off the old templates once the switch is done so both are not sent.\n- Item dev-deadline-end-of-month:item:6 was a stated remark about deleting them from the sender config after a day of clean sends.\n- Item dev-deadline-end-of-month:item:7 was a stated request for a preview link for the referral block.\n- Item dev-deadline-end-of-month:item:8 was a stated remark about sending one this afternoon.\n- Item dev-deadline-end-of-month:item:9 was a stated remark about not being able to change the referral wording after this week.\n- Item dev-deadline-end-of-month:item:10 was a stated suggestion to keep that wording frozen."
